## Why this precedes the large validator

- It directly tests whether complete transaction, prefix, no-refire, and
  resource consistency select physical odds.
- It closes token-to-successor control at the same literal-factor standard as
  Blocks 23--30 if green.
- It is much cheaper than compiling hundreds of pointer controls and exact
  stochastic dilations before knowing whether those details can affect the
  law fork.
- It exposes the exact remaining selector if the interval survives.

